    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d671">

                <pb facs="0702" n="604" xml:id="pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5397: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-27T17:00:00-05:00">October 27, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>368. Department’s instruction 216, August 15.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Department has received a letter from the bank in question<anchor
                            n="58" xml:id="d671-f1"/> transmitting newspaper report that the Chinese
                        Government has asked foreign ministers to send representatives to Nanking to
                        discuss action in connection with defaulted obligations. The bank indicates
                        its willingness to consider sending a representative if the American
                        Minister should think this desirable.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Please report by telegraph whether note has been despatched in accordance
                        with Department’s instruction of August 15 and add comments on subjects
                        mentioned above.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
